{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.557045265Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7cc502dc","body":"BiologySnapshot struct in crates/tank_api/src/handlers/snapshot.rs (line 144-162) is missing the sub_adult_count field. TankSnapshot now has sub_adult_count (snapshot.rs:39) and it's populated from state.animal.sub_adult.count (snapshot.rs:138), but the /biology API endpoint silently omits sub-adults. Add `pub sub_adult_count: u32` to BiologySnapshot and populate it from `s.sub_adult_count` in get_biology().","dedup_key":"eefbe8d65660bb5c717638a030981d4b29b76bce8e25bba81ae3107f8a1fd5d1","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.565651539Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-84c60567","body":"The conductivity calculation in crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs:174 uses a bare magic number 0.65 (`self.tds_mg_per_l(volume_l) / 0.65`). Per the project prompt's requirement that 'conversion factors should be defined as named constants, not magic numbers scattered through rendering code', this should be a named constant (e.g., `const TDS_TO_CONDUCTIVITY_FACTOR: f64 = 0.65;`) with a doc comment explaining its derivation and limitations.","dedup_key":"dceeb4cce5eaa895d52e1607152c4a231cfb44db6306e697690654ddc147d162","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":16,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.575987895Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-6e910aa8","body":"The chemistry_field_semantics metadata (snapshot.rs:100-112) only documents the new-style field names. It should also document `do_mg_l` and `do_sat_mg_l` (which appear in the chemistry response at lines 57-58) since these lack the explicit unit suffix pattern used by other fields and could be confused with dissolved organic matter.","dedup_key":"22423b71787a474adca483d3c4e798060fc4641494ce538e23e9195208781dcc","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":17,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.584612884Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-59fbe31e","body":"The GH/KH conversion constants in water.rs (lines 5-6, and the inline coefficients 2.497 and 4.118 at line 162) are bare magic numbers without documentation of their chemical derivation. Like the N/P conversion factors in conversions.rs, these should be named constants with doc comments explaining the molar mass ratios they represent (Ca²+ equivalent weight → CaCO3, Mg²+ equivalent weight → CaCO3).","dedup_key":"a645dcd12b1d9dad3a8c5d10a63c95f68c4725f7c29afdeffbb80a67ec23f326","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":18,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.593274242Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-85925171","body":"`snapshot_response_json()` only backfills legacy aliases for TAN/NH3/NO2/NO3/PO4/TDS/conductivity in `crates/tank_api/src/handlers/snapshot.rs:86-96`, but `TankSnapshot` also renamed `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_l` to `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_per_l` in `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:20-21`. As a result, `/snapshot`, `/time/step`, `/load`, and scenario-load responses no longer contain the old DIC key, so pre-rename API clients that deserialize the old snapshot shape will fail even though the other renamed fields were kept backward-compatible. Add the missing top-level `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_l` alias and include it in `legacy_chemistry_aliases`.","dedup_key":"46c603871e84a8b8e5f485c2f724e9ef6df95e310bc35bd5bbb13fb3bc147141","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":19,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.601875286Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-3f440546","body":"`OMITTED_TDS_CONTRIBUTORS` in `crates/tank_api/src/handlers/snapshot.rs:9-12` says the 7-ion estimate omits \"untracked nitrogen and phosphorus ions\". That is false for this model: TAN/NH3, nitrite, nitrate, and phosphate are tracked and surfaced in the same response; they are merely excluded from the TDS/conductivity proxy. Reword this metadata to say those tracked species are omitted from the estimate, otherwise the new self-description still misstates model scope and can mislead users about what the simulation actually tracks.","dedup_key":"ef46eb9a4dff7b06a0eceb39a0289a2ce6b7f3769d2224dbfbe37b6592d3bf8b","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":20,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:50:17.610525964Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9ac0386b","body":"`crates/tank_tui/src/screens/chemistry.rs:51-59` and `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/overview.rs:49-58` stop at `Est. TDS (7-ion)` / `Est. conductivity`, but never tell the TUI user which seven ions are counted or that nitrate/phosphate/organics are excluded. The API now carries that scope metadata, so the UI portion of this bead is still incomplete: a TUI user cannot actually tell what the estimate includes or omits, which was part of the acceptance criteria for the chemistry-semantics change.","dedup_key":"bbb919c1a096488880496d63d1c4d0ac6c402a3ee047fb681609036491602e94","run_id":"run-20260328125529","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
